Workstream ID: career-graph
Title: Genuine 3D career graph, focus-first visibility and view controls
Status: DONE
Milestone: Inspect real saved relationships without inventing work or clutter
Dependencies: tracker-foundation
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/4
Purpose: Record the implemented Three.js graph and its final mission-only,
  focus-first behavior. Earlier superseded visual experiments remain source history,
  not separate claims that rejected behavior is still the target.

Tasks:
  [x] Render real nodes/relationships with actual 3D camera, picking and inspection.
  [x] Keep mission rings separate from work totals and collection metadata.
  [x] Show inactive isolated hubs; actual completion today reveals that mission.
  [x] Add reversible Show everything without changing focus/progress.
  [x] Redistribute crowded mission/stage fans with effective node spacing.
  [x] Provide individual ring speeds, Labels and independent dot/line spark amounts.
  [x] Keep heartbeat deformation, reduced motion and lifecycle cleanup consistent.

Acceptance criteria:
  Connections represent documented relationships, never keyword-invented prerequisites.
  Quiet hubs have no incident connections or checkpoint clouds by default.
  Today's background-completion reveal expires without activating a mission.
  View controls are presentation-only; both spark percentages default to 10.
  Per-ring speed is phase-continuous; quiet/global motion rules still apply.

Completion evidence:
  Retrospective authored: 2026-11-06.
  Public revisions: 8cf0889, efdc7e6, 091d751, 4011304, dc639cc, 71cc430,
    2c3e4e7, 78e0732 and fixture-only e42528e/9b2903b.
